---
description: Prefer self-explanatory code over comments
alwaysApply: true
---

# No comments by default

Do not add comments to code unless the user explicitly asks for them.

- Prefer clear names, small functions, and structure that explain intent
- Do not leave narrating, leftover, or “explainer” comments
- Avoid TODO / FIXME comments unless the user requests them
- JSDoc is allowed only when a public API truly needs a type-level contract that TypeScript cannot express
